      "body": "## Purpose\nFix a silent tool-call drop in the Llama-4 pythonic tool parser.\n\n## Problem\nIn `Llama4PythonicToolParser.extract_tool_calls` (non-streaming), the `<|python_end|>` removal is nested **inside** the `if model_output.startswith(\"<|python_start|>\")` block:\n```python\nif model_output.startswith(\"<|python_start|>\"):\n    model_output = model_output[len(\"<|python_start|>\") :]\n    model_output = model_output.replace(\"<|python_end|>\", \"\")   # only runs with a start token\n```\nWhen a Llama-4 response emits `<|python_end|>` **without** a leading `<|python_start|>`, the sentinel survives → `ast.parse` raises `SyntaxError` → the exception is swallowed → the tool call is silently dropped.\n\nRepro: `model_output = \"[get_weather(city='Paris')]<|python_end|>\"`\n- Current: `tools_called=False`, call lost.\n- Expected: `tools_called=True`, one `get_weather(city='Paris')` call.\n\nThe **streaming** path (same file) already strips `<|python_end|>` unconditionally, so the two paths disagree on identical input — strong evidence this is an unintended bug (the module comment even notes Llama 4 \"sometime will output those tokens\").\n\n## Fix\nDedent the `<|python_end|>` strip so it runs regardless of the start token, matching the streaming path.\n\n## Test\nAdded a parametrized non-streaming case `end_token_without_start_nonstreaming` to `tests/tool_parsers/test_llama4_pythonic_tool_parser.py` asserting the call is still extracted. It fails before the fix (call dropped) and passes after.\n\n*(Note: verified the parse-path divergence with an isolated reproduction of the exact strip + regex + `ast.parse` logic; vLLM's full test env needs the CUDA/torch stack, so the parametrized test runs in CI.)*\n\n---\n*Developed with AI assistance (Claude Code): the path divergence was located, the one-line dedent applied, and verified locally. I reviewed and verified the change and take responsibility for it.*\n",
